    <s:String x:Key="Str.SectionAbout">About</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.AboutLine1">FPS Tune is a system-level frame rate optimizer for Windows, aimed at all FPS games.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.AboutLine2">It only adjusts Windows system-level settings: it does not modify game files, inject into processes, interact with anti-cheat, disable boot virtualization or spoof the GPU. Every change is backed up before it is written and can be restored in one click.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.CheckUpdate">Check for updates</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.GitHubHome">GitHub page</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.NotChecked">Not checked</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.ContactNote">Contact is for cooperation and feedback only.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.DlssOverrideNote">Override preset (applies to the currently located game; if you also pick an upscaling option in game, this override wins)</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.PresetK">K preset (recommended)</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.PresetKDesc">New-generation model · widely used, stable</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.FollowGameDesc">No override; the in-game setting decides</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.PresetLatestDesc">Evolves automatically with driver updates</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.PresetM">M preset</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.PresetMDesc">New-generation model · first choice for high-end image quality</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.PresetJ">J preset</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.PresetJDesc">New-generation model · earlier version</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.PresetE">E preset</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.PresetEDesc">Previous-generation CNN model · retro image quality</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.DlssNote">Note: the override is written to a driver profile this tool creates, and deleting it restores everything. Profiles you or NVIDIA App created are never touched. You have to get in game to judge the visual difference.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.VibNote">Applies to the whole screen (desktop, browser and games all become more vivid), not just in game. Streamers commonly use 70–80%.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.VibNote2">Note: the current level is remembered before any change, and Restore original brings it back in one click. Independent of the ICC filter, and the two can be combined. If colour accuracy matters to you, use a lower level or keep the default.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.IccPresetLabel">Presets (applied to the primary monitor for the whole desktop: desktop, browser and game windows)</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.IccVivid">Vivid FPS</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.IccVividDesc">Slightly higher saturation and contrast, good for competitive play</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.IccShadow">Shadow boost</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.IccShadowDesc">Lifts the shadow range, prioritising dark corners</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.IccDehaze">Dehaze</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.IccDehazeDesc">S-curve contrast with slightly reduced blue, for foggy scenes</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.IccStandard">Standard</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.IccStandardDesc">Restores your original colour configuration</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.IccNote">Note: the generated ICC is a simple curve transform and is weaker than professional calibration; if colour accuracy matters to you, keep your original profile. Returning here and choosing Standard or Restore original brings everything back. Multiple monitors are not supported yet.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.DrsNote">Written into the same per-game profile as the DLSS override, sharing one Restore default. SettingIDs come from NVIDIA's official NvApiDriverSettings.h. The recommended values cross-check high-frequency community guides (Douyin / Bilibili / guide sites, September 2026).</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.TipOneClickEsports">High-quality textures + prefer maximum performance + 2x transparency AA + 1 prerendered frame; on high-end desktop cards transparency AA is raised to 4x automatically</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.DrsDefaultHint">Recommended: high-quality textures · 2x transparency AA · 1 prerendered frame</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.DrsTextureFilter">Texture filtering · quality</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.TipTextureFilter">On modern Nvidia cards High quality costs almost nothing in frame rate and makes distant textures clearly sharper (recommended)</s:String>
